    #      specs/0025's blob at P4's doc commit, efdacd5c. The working file is
    #      printed (equal to the pin while planning holds nothing uncommitted),
    #      and the status pattern still allows it modified, should planning add
    #      rulings mid-phase. The pattern allows this phase's logs and its
    #      records/m3p3-p4- and records/m3p3-open- stems.
    #  KB. Three families, P1's S0 to S3C, P2's P0 to P3C and P3's Q0 to F3C, one
    #      generator gen-p4.py written for this phase from P1's gen-p1.py, P2's
    #      gen-p2.py and P3's gen-p3.py: the template's sheetData given root
    #      children before it (S), after it (P), or rows, children, a
    #      relationships prefix, a worksheet relationships part and a table part
    #      (Q). The expected lines are the three earlier logs' (S_NONE, S_PR,
    #      S_VIEWS; P_NONE, P_SETUP, P_BOTH, P_HF; Q_PLAIN, Q_BOUND, Q_FILTER).
    #      The part's write message is reached six ways; the overlap, the index
    #      and part 3's two-elements messages, shared with earlier parts, apart.
    #  KC. The part's messages and the seven bodies are P3's; no source change
    #      of this phase touches them (the carry is test code, the catalogue //!
    #      lines, the probes the size-probe crate). TWO_ELEMENTS joins
    #      TABLE_OVERLAP and INDEX_OUT_OF_RANGE among the messages read apart.
    #      "a sheet setting is out of range", "a header or footer text is not
    #      valid" and "a print area or title is not valid" are stated unreachable
    #      through the tool (each sample's settings, texts and title pair are its
    #      constants), each with the crate tests that cover it and each test's
    #      body asserted to hold the message. The overlap message is looked for in
    #      the working spec, which now equals the committed one: "Planning rulings
    #      during P3" ruling 1 quotes it there.
    #  KD. Nothing of P3's carried rules is dropped. This script removes no
    #      directory: the worktree goes by git worktree remove, the scratch
    #      directory is kept on the disk under <build>, and no rm of any form is
    #      run.
    #
    # P3's text:
    # Milestone 3 part 3 P3 negative.log (specs/0025-sheet-and-print-settings.md,
    # "P3": "The negative log through the binary: the sample on a fixture whose
    # first sheet's table covers A1:H2 (refused with the overlap message, with a
    # control)"). One family, --printarea-sample, the gate's host debug binary
    # copied into a detached worktree of the phase commit and checked against
    # gate.log's hash, on fictional packages this log builds from the phase
    # commit's template files. The template's worksheet holds an empty sheetData
    # alone, so M is 0 and the sample's area is A1:H1 unless a case adds rows:
    #
    # (Q) --printarea-sample:
    #       Q0 the bare template: the three names and the <autoFilter> created,
    #          exit 0, its line;
    #       T1 a table part on W whose ref is A1:H2, over the area: specs/0021's
    #          overlap message, "a table overlaps a table, a pivot table, a merge
    #          or the autofilter", from the write's check of W's tables;
    #       T1C the same table at A3:H9, clear of the area, the control for T1;
    #       A2 two <autoFilter> after the sheetData: the part's message, "a
    #          worksheet has two sheetPr, autoFilter, printOptions, ...", from the
    #          settings pass;
    #       A2C one <autoFilter>, the control for A2;
    #       F3 a row 1048576 with a cell, so M + 1 is past the grid: part 3's
    #          index message, from the print area call;
    #       F3C a row 2 with a cell, the control for F3.
    # Each refusal: exit 2, the error line exactly the message the committed
    # source holds, no stdout, no output file. Then the part's messages, read from
    # the source by constant name, compared as SETS with those reached here and
    # those the log states unreachable, each unreachable one with its reason and
    # the tests that cover it; the two shared messages reached here apart; and
    # usage shapes.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 3 P3 from M3 part 3 P2's negative script (printed in
    # records/logs/m3p3-p2/negative.log, byte-identical to its copy kept on the
    # disk as <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p3-p3/gen/negative-template-m3p3-p2.sh;
    # its change lists, P2's IA to ID and the earlier ones, follow below). Every
    # check, control and helper of the frame is that text's. What differs, and
    # why:
    #  JA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects and the build directories
    #      are M3 part 3 P3's. The base is M3 part 3 P2's record commit ("M3 part
    #      3 P2 record:"); the doc commit and the three code commits (the carry,
    #      the crate, the tool) by their full P3 subjects. The spec pin is
    #      specs/0025's blob at P3's doc commit, 338f0e8b. The working file is
    #      printed, and the status pattern allows it modified: planning holds
    #      "Planning rulings during P3" uncommitted. The pattern allows this
    #      phase's logs and its records/m3p3-p3- and records/m3p3-open- stems.
    #  JB. One family, Q0 to F3C, the generator gen-p3.py written for this phase:
    #      the template's sheetData given rows, root children after it, a
    #      relationships prefix on the root, a worksheet relationships part and a
    #      table part, as each case needs. The part's write message reached by
    #      two autoFilter; the overlap and index messages, shared with earlier
    #      parts, reached apart, each with its control.
    #  JC. The part's messages are the constants package.rs defines under the
    #      Cargo feature sheetprops and under sheetprops and metadata together
    #      (gated.py now takes the cfg's text), compared as a SET with the
    #      constants seven bodies return: P2's six and Parts::set_print_titles;
    #      set_print_area and set_auto_filter return the shared index message
    #      alone and are not among them. "a sheet setting is out of range", "a
    #      header or footer text is not valid" and "a print area or title is not
    #      valid" are stated unreachable through the tool (the sample makes no
    #      settings or header call, and its title pair is its constant), each
    #      with the crate tests that cover it and each test's body asserted to
    #      hold the message. TABLE_OVERLAP and INDEX_OUT_OF_RANGE are read by
    #      name apart, each once and not empty; the overlap message is looked for
    #      in the working spec, where "Planning rulings during P3" ruling 1 quotes
    #      it, the committed spec misquoting it (printed, not asserted).
    #  JD. Nothing of P2's carried rules is dropped. This script removes no
    #      directory: the worktree goes by git worktree remove, the scratch
    #      directory is kept on the disk under <build>, and no rm of any form is
    #      run (specs/0024 P2 ruling 1 needs none here).
    #
    # P2's text:
    # Milestone 3 part 3 P2 negative.log (specs/0025-sheet-and-print-settings.md,
    # "P2": "The negative log through the binary: the sample on a fixture with two
    # <pageSetup> (refused, with a control)"). One family, --pagesetup-sample, the
    # gate's host debug binary copied into a detached worktree of the phase commit
    # and checked against gate.log's hash, on fictional packages this log builds
    # from the phase commit's template files. The template's worksheet holds an
    # empty sheetData alone (none of the four elements the sample sets, no
    # sheetPr), its root binds no relationships prefix:
    #
    # (P) --pagesetup-sample:
    #       P0 the bare template: <sheetPr>, <printOptions>, <pageMargins>,
    #          <pageSetup> and <headerFooter> all created, exit 0, its line;
    #       P1 two <pageSetup/> after the sheetData: the part's message, "a
    #          worksheet has two sheetPr, autoFilter, printOptions, ...", from the
    #          settings pass;
    #       P1C one <pageSetup/>, the control for P1;
    #       P2 a <pageSetup/> and then a <pageMargins/>, the pageMargins out of
    #          schema order: the same message;
    #       P2C the <pageMargins/> before the <pageSetup/>, the control for P2;
    #       P3 two <headerFooter/>: the same message;
    #       P3C one <headerFooter/>, the control for P3.
    # Each refusal: exit 2, the error line exactly the message the committed
    # source holds, no stdout, no output file. Then the part's messages, read from
    # the source by constant name, compared as SETS with those reached here and
    # those the log states unreachable, each unreachable one with its reason and
    # the tests that cover it; and usage shapes.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 3 P2 from M3 part 3 P1's negative script (printed in
    # records/logs/m3p3-p1/negative.log, byte-identical to its copy kept on the
    # disk as <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p3-p2/gen/negative-template-m3p3-p1.sh;
    # its change lists, P1's HA to HD and the earlier ones, follow below). Every
    # check, control and helper of the frame is that text's. What differs, and
    # why:
    #  IA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects and the build directories
    #      are M3 part 3 P2's. The base is M3 part 3 P1's record commit ("M3 part
    #      3 P1 record:"); the doc commit and the three code commits (the carry,
    #      the crate, the tool) by their full P2 subjects. The spec pin is
    #      specs/0025's blob at P2's doc commit, 6c6e87e3. The working file is
    #      printed, and the status pattern allows it modified: planning holds
    #      "Planning rulings during P2" uncommitted. The pattern allows this
    #      phase's logs and its records/m3p3-p2- and records/m3p3-open- stems.
    #  IB. One family, P0 to P3C, the generator gen-p2.py written for this phase:
    #      the template's sheetData given a tail of root children after it. The
    #      part's write message reached three ways (two pageSetup, one out of
    #      order, two headerFooter), each with its control. P1's apart record of
    #      part 3's two-elements message is dropped: no case here reaches it.
    #  IC. The part's messages are the constants package.rs defines under the
    #      Cargo feature sheetprops, compared as a SET with the constants the six
    #      bodies return: Parts::set_tab_color, set_sheet_view,
    #      set_page_margins, set_page_setup and set_header_footer (the private
    #      fns) and SettingsPass::observe; set_print_options records with no
    #      check and has no private body. "a sheet setting is out of range" and
    #      "a header or footer text is not valid" are stated unreachable through
    #      the tool (the sample's settings and texts are its constants), each
    #      with the crate tests that cover it and each test's body asserted to
    #      hold the message.
    #  ID. Nothing of P1's carried rules is dropped. This script removes no
    #      directory: the worktree goes by git worktree remove, the scratch
    #      directory is kept on the disk under <build>, and no rm of any form is
    #      run (specs/0024 P2 ruling 1 needs none here).
    #
    # P1's text:
    # Milestone 3 part 3 P1 negative.log (specs/0025-sheet-and-print-settings.md,
    # "P1": "The negative log through the binary: the sample on a fixture with two
    # <sheetPr> (refused, with a control)"). One family, --sheetview-sample, the
    # gate's host debug binary copied into a detached worktree of the phase commit
    # and checked against gate.log's hash, on fictional packages this log builds
    # from the phase commit's template files. The template's worksheet holds an
    # empty sheetData alone (no sheetPr, no dimension, no sheetViews), its root
    # binds no relationships prefix:
    #
    # (S) --sheetview-sample:
    #       S0 the bare template: <sheetPr> and <sheetViews> both created, exit 0,
    #          its line;
    #       S1 two <sheetPr/> before the sheetData: the part's new message, "a
    #          worksheet has two sheetPr, ...", from the settings pass;
    #       S1C one <sheetPr/>, the control for S1;
    #       S2 a <dimension> and then a <sheetPr/>, the sheetPr out of schema
    #          order: the same message;
    #       S2C the <sheetPr/> before the <dimension>, the control for S2;
    #       S3 two <sheetViews>, each holding one <sheetView>: part 3's message
    #          for two cols, sheetViews or mergeCells elements;
    #       S3C one <sheetViews>, the control for S3.
    # Each refusal: exit 2, the error line exactly the message the committed
    # source holds, no stdout, no output file. Then the part's messages, read from
    # the source by constant name, compared as SETS with those reached here and
    # those the log states unreachable, the unreachable one with its reason and
    # the test that covers it; and usage shapes.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 3 P1 from M3 part 2 P3's negative script (printed in
    # records/logs/m3p2-p3/negative.log, byte-identical to its copy kept on the
    # disk under <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p2-p3/scripts, which this phase keeps
    # as <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p3-p1/gen/negative-template-m3p2-p3.sh; its
    # change lists GA to GD stand in that log). Every check, control and helper
    # of the frame is that text's (the entry and exit checks, the shape greps,
    # the role checks, the roots, the gate binary's copy and hash, the message
    # reader messages.py and the body reader returns.py with their controls, the
    # spec lookup, run_bin and its predicates, the set comparison, the usage
    # shapes, the byte count, the status and stderr checks). What differs, and
    # why:
    #  HA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects and the build directories
    #      are M3 part 3 P1's. The base is M3 part 2's close-out record commit
    #      ("M3 part 2 close-out record:"); the doc commit and the three code
    #      commits (the carry, the crate, the tool) by their full P1 subjects.
    #      The spec pin is specs/0025's blob at P1's doc commit, c15d68d2. The
    #      working file is printed, and the status pattern allows it modified:
    #      planning holds "Planning rulings during P1" uncommitted. The pattern
    #      allows this phase's logs and its records/m3p3-p1- and records/m3p3-open-
    #      stems.
    #  HB. One family, S0 to S3C, the generator gen-p1.py written for this phase:
    #      the template's sheetData given a head of root children before it. The
    #      new write message reached two ways (two sheetPr, one out of order),
    #      part 3's message once (two sheetViews), each with its control.
    #  HC. The part's messages are the constants package.rs defines under the
    #      Cargo feature sheetprops (a reader printed below takes each const
    #      whose line follows #[cfg(feature = "sheetprops")]), compared as a SET
    #      with the constants the three bodies return: Parts::set_tab_color,
    #      Parts::set_sheet_view (the private fns) and SettingsPass::observe.
    #      Part 3's two-elements message is recorded apart (as P3 recorded the
    #      index message), since it is not the part's. "a sheet setting is out of
    #      range" is stated unreachable through the tool (the sample's colour and
    #      zoom are its constants), with the crate test that covers it and the
    #      test's body asserted to hold the message. "Errors"' other shared
    #      messages are every edit's, not the sample's constants, and earlier
    #      parts' negative logs reach them; they are printed, not accounted.
    #  HD. Nothing of P3's carried rules is dropped. This script removes no
    #      directory: the worktree goes by git worktree remove, the scratch
    #      directory is kept on the disk under <build>, and no rm of any form is
    #      run (specs/0024 P2 ruling 1 needs none here).
    #
    # Usage: m6p6-p3-negative.sh <phase commit> [<gate log>] [<size log>] > <file
    # outside the tree>, PLANNING_SPEC set to the working spec's sha256 (and
    # SIZE_BUILD_ROOT for a dry run's size build); the caller moves the output to
    # records/logs/m6p6-p3/negative.log. Run after the size log (ruling P).
    set -uo pipefail
    SELF_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
    SELF=$SELF_DIR/$(basename "$0")
    # specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7: this script's own standard error, kept and counted at the end.
    mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out" || exit 2
    ERR=$SELF_DIR/out/negative.stderr
    exec 2>"$ERR"
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    unset EMEND_CORPUS_DIR EMEND_KEEP_DIR RUSTDOCFLAGS RUSTFLAGS CARGO_TARGET_DIR
    # Change MJ: P2 verification ruling 6, and every script's offline cargo
    # setting (this log runs no cargo), each printed as an input line.
    export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
    export CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true
    PHASE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m6p6-p3
    # Change MB: the gate's log and build directory, whose host debug
    # emend-copy copy this log runs.
    GATE_LOG=${2:-$PHASE_DIR/logs/gate.log}
    GATE_BUILD=${GATE_BUILD_ROOT:-$PHASE_DIR/gate}
    GATE_BIN=$GATE_BUILD/bin/host/emend-copy
    # Change NE60 (specs/0043 rulings O and P): N8's runs take the size log's
    # release binaries, both labels: the size log (the third argument, or
    # <phase>/logs/size.log) and its build directory (<target>/main unless
    # SIZE_BUILD_ROOT names a dry run's), the binaries checked against the
    # hash lines the size log prints. So this log runs after the size log.
    SIZE_LOG=${3:-$PHASE_DIR/logs/size.log}
    SIZE_BUILD=${SIZE_BUILD_ROOT:-$PHASE_DIR/target/main}
    BUILD_ROOT=${NEGATIVE_BUILD:-$PHASE_DIR/negative}
    SUPERSEDED_DIR=$PHASE_DIR/superseded
    TARGET_DIR=$PHASE_DIR/target
    SPEC=specs/0043-measurement-and-close.md
    # Change NC55: M6 part 4's spec, read at the phase commit and in its
    # working file for the message it quotes (NO_SERIES_AT's, change NC53).
    SPEC41=specs/0041-chart-text-and-edits.md
    # Change NA47: part 2's spec, read at the phase commit and in its working
    # file for the range message it quotes (change NC44's checks).
    P2SPEC=specs/0039-chart-kinds-and-formatting.md
    # Change NA44: part 1's spec, read at the phase commit and in its working
    # file for the messages it quotes (part 1's three and N8's; change NC44).
    P1SPEC=specs/0038-chartsheets.md
    SPEC_WANT=cc1b5d902817c7fd9b792aa56c8a5cdfb9b4132cc71e228ed2759415c550addc
    # Change NA60: the working spec holds planning's rulings written during
    # M6 part 6 P3 (M to P) and not yet committed; PLANNING_SPEC names its
    # sha256, and the working file is checked against it below (P3's doc
    # commit committed specs/0043 at cc1b5d90).
    PLANNING_SPEC=${PLANNING_SPEC:-}
    mkdir -p "$BUILD_ROOT" || exit 2
    # Change MP (close-out ruling 1): TMPDIR is <build>/tmp, written
    # <scratch>/tmp, made before any mktemp; every mktemp below takes it.
    TMPDIR=$BUILD_ROOT/tmp
    export TMPDIR
    mkdir -p "$TMPDIR" || exit 2
    # Change HC: this run's own directory, removed at the end (in TMPDIR,
    # change MP).
    B=$(mktemp -d) || exit 2
    git show "$C:scripts/counting.sh" >"$B/counting.sh" || exit 2
    . "$B/counting.sh"
    fail=0
    check() { echo "  $1: $2"; [ "$2" = yes ] || fail=1; }
    yn() { if "$@"; then echo yes; else echo no; fi; }
    # For a condition that must NOT hold: a leading bang inside yn runs a
    # command named by the bang (specs/0001), so a negation has its own helper.
    ynnot() { if "$@"; then echo no; else echo yes; fi; }
    
    head_is() { [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$1" ]; }
    full_sha() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; }
    # The given commit is the phase commit when it is a full sha and HEAD.
    given_ok() { full_sha "$1" && head_is "$1"; }
    if given_ok "$C"; then :; else echo "the phase commit must be a full 40-hex sha that is HEAD, not $C" >&2; exit 2; fi
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    case "${C: -1}" in 0) LAST=1 ;; *) LAST=0 ;; esac
    FAKE_SHA=${C:0:39}$LAST
    SHORT_SHA=${C:0:7}
    # What the status pattern admits (M4 part 2 P1 verification ruling 3; changes
    # NA31 to NA60): this phase's logs, this phase's records (the sheet,
    # chartsheet and copy samples' rerun pairs, the open pair, the size record
    # and the API listing, named by the phase commit's short sha,
    # untracked) and planning's modified specs/0043 and ROADMAP.md; nothing
    # else.
    OURS="^((\\?\\?| ?[MARCD]) records/logs/m6p6-p3/|\\?\\? records/((m6p6-p3-(sheet|chartsheet|copy)|m6p6-open)-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-$SHORT_SHA[.](md|txt)|(size-m6p6|api-review-m6p6)-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-$SHORT_SHA[.]md)\$| M specs/0043-measurement-and-close[.]md\$| M ROADMAP[.]md\$)"
    entry_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    entry_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    entry_clean() { [ "$entry_all" != error ] && [ "$entry_ours" != error ] && [ "$entry_all" = "$entry_ours" ]; }
    if entry_clean; then :; else
      echo "the working tree holds changes outside this phase's logs, its record pairs and planning's modified spec and roadmap" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    
    scrub() {
      sed -e "s#$MAIN#<repo>#g" -e "s#$SELF_DIR#<scripts>#g" -e "s#$B#<scratch>/w#g" -e "s#$TMPDIR#<scratch>/tmp#g" \
        -e "s#$BUILD_ROOT#<build>#g" -e "s#$GATE_BUILD#<gatebuild>#g" -e "s#$SUPERSEDED_DIR#<superseded>#g" \
        -e "s#$TARGET_DIR#<target>#g" -e "s#$PHASE_DIR#<phase>#g" \
        -e "s#$HOME#<home>#g"
    }
    exec 3>&1
    exec > >(scrub >&3)
    SCRUB_PID=$!
    
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    echo "invocation: bash <scripts>/$(basename "$0") $*"
    echo "input: RERUN_NOTE: ${RERUN_NOTE:-unset}"
    echo "input: RERUN_FILES: ${RERUN_FILES:-unset}"
    echo "input: PLANNING_SPEC: ${PLANNING_SPEC:-unset} (the working spec's sha256, planning's rulings during M6 part 6 P3; change NA60)"
    echo "input: the size log: $SIZE_LOG (the third argument, or <phase>/logs/size.log; its release binaries run N8's cases; change NE60)"
    echo "input (environment) SIZE_BUILD_ROOT: ${SIZE_BUILD_ROOT:+set, a dry run's}${SIZE_BUILD_ROOT:-unset, so the size log's build directory is <target>/main} (change NE60)"
    echo "input: PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE: ${PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE:-unset} (exported 1 by this script; P2 verification ruling 6; change MJ)"
    echo "input: CARGO_NET_OFFLINE: ${CARGO_NET_OFFLINE:-unset} (exported true by this script; this log runs no cargo; change MJ)"
    echo "input: TMPDIR=<scratch>/tmp (exported by this script before any mktemp: <build>/tmp, made if missing; close-out ruling 1; change MP)"
    echo "input: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo set || echo unset) (its value never printed)"
    echo "input: HOME: set, read for the paths under it, printed as <home>"
    echo "input: NEGATIVE_BUILD: ${NEGATIVE_BUILD:-unset} (the build root, <build>)"
    echo "input: the gate log: $GATE_LOG (the second argument, or <phase>/logs/gate.log; change MB)"
    echo "input (environment) GATE_BUILD_ROOT: ${GATE_BUILD_ROOT:+set; <gatebuild> below is it, a dry run}${GATE_BUILD_ROOT:-unset, so <gatebuild> is <phase>/gate} (change MB)"
    echo "about: M6 part 6 P3 phase commit $C; HEAD at run: $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    echo "names: in the carried checks' text, P1 to P4 with no part named are Milestone 5 part 5's phases and part 4 is Milestone 5 part 4, as M5 part 5 P4 wrote them; where M6 part 1's carried text says this phase it is part 1 P1 (B4, N6, N7 and its three constants), P2 (N8) or P3 (N9); where M6 part 2 P1's says it, it is part 2 P1 (B5, N10, CHART_VALUE_RANGE and the surface and of-pie rules); where M6 part 2 P2's says it, it is part 2 P2 (B6, N11, the marker, line and point ranges and rules); where part 2 P3's says it, part 2 P3 (no case); where part 3 P1's says it, part 3 P1 (B7, N12, the trendline and error bar rules); where part 3 P2's says it, part 3 P2 (B8, N13, the plot line and axis rules); where part 3 P3's says it, part 3 P3 (no case); where M6 part 4 P1's says it, it is M6 part 4 P1 (B9, N14, the text rules); where M6 part 4 P2's says it, it is M6 part 4 P2 (B10, N15, the edit rules and NO_SERIES_AT); where M6 part 4 P3's says it, it is M6 part 4 P3 (no case); where M6 part 5 P1's says it, it is M6 part 5 P1 (B11 to B13, N16 to N19 and the gradient rules); where M6 part 5 P2's says it, it is M6 part 5 P2 (B14, N20 to N23, the named style rules, STYLE_NAME_REFUSED and TWO_CONTAINERS's new text); where M6 part 5 P3's says it, it is M6 part 5 P3 (no case); this phase, M6 part 6 P3, turns N8 into ruling M's accepting case and adds N8P, its control (specs/0043 rulings M, O and P; change NA60)"
    echo
    echo "## the three shape greps, over this script, before its log (specs/0001)"
    D='$'
    SHAPE_CHAIN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) .*(&&|\\|\\|)"
    SHAPE_BANG="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) !"
    SHAPE_ASSIGN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*="
    P3=python3
    # Change MQ: a Python call is a line that is not a comment where python3
    # is followed by whitespace and an option, `-` or a path ending .py; PYB
    # counts those without `-I -B` after python3.
    PY_CALL="^[[:space:]]*([^#[:space:]].*[^-[:alnum:]_/.])?${P3}[[:space:]]+(-|[^[:space:]]+[.]py)"
    PY_IB="${P3}[[:space:]]+-I[[:space:]]+-B([[:space:]]|\$)"
    # pyb_count <file>: the calls in <file> without -I -B.
    pyb_count() { LC_ALL=C "$G" -E "$PY_CALL" "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -cvE "$PY_IB"; }
    printf '%s\n' "x=${D}(is [ 1 ] && true)" "y=${D}(isnot ! true)" "z=${D}(yn N=1 true)" "  ${P3} -c 'x'" "  ${P3} -I -B -c 'x'" "# ${P3} -c 'x'" "command -v ${P3}" >"$B/shape-fixture"
    echo "command: count_matches -E <shape> <this script>, and the same over a fixture holding one line of each shape; for PYB, the call form then the lines without -I -B"
    for shape in CHAIN BANG ASSIGN PYB; do
      if [ "$shape" = PYB ]; then
        n_self=$(pyb_count "$SELF")
        n_fix=$(pyb_count "$B/shape-fixture")
      else
        var=SHAPE_$shape
        n_self=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$SELF")
        n_fix=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$B/shape-fixture")
      fi
      echo "  shape $shape: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
      check "$shape: this script holds none" "$(yn [ "$n_self" = 0 ])"
      check "control: $shape: the same form finds the fixture's one line" "$(yn [ "$n_fix" = 1 ])"
    done
    n_calls_fix=$(count_matches -E "$PY_CALL" "$B/shape-fixture")
    echo "  Python calls in the fixture by the call form: $n_calls_fix (the one without -I -B and the one with; the comment and command -v are not calls)"
    check "control: the call form counts the fixture's two calls and neither the comment nor command -v" "$(yn [ "$n_calls_fix" = 2 ])"
    check "control: ynnot reports no on a passing command" "$(yn [ "$(ynnot true)" = no ])"
    # Change NF41 (rulings Z and AD, specs/0038 "Generator rules"; ruling AK a):
    # the defined-helper check over this script's own source, gen/defined.py's
    # program carried here with is and isnot read as yn and ynnot are, with its
    # planted controls; and yn and ynnot themselves defined. The planted calls
    # are built from pieces, so this text holds no call of an undefined name.
    cat >"$B/defined.py" <<'DEFINED'
    import re
    import sys
    
    CALL = re.compile(r"\$\((?:yn|ynnot|is|isnot) ([^ )\"]+)")
    WRAP = re.compile(r"\$\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) ")
    DEF = re.compile(r"^[ \t]*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\(\) \{", re.M)
    
    
    def calls(script, form):
        called = set()
        for line in script.split("\n"):
            if line.lstrip().startswith("#"):
                continue
            called.update(form.findall(line))
        return called
    
    
    commands = sys.argv[1].split()
    for path in sys.argv[2:]:
        name = path.rsplit("/", 1)[-1]
        text = open(path, encoding="utf-8").read()
        defined = set(DEF.findall(text))
        called = calls(text, CALL)
        missing = sorted(n for n in called if n not in commands and n not in defined)
        wcalled = sorted(calls(text, WRAP))
        wmissing = [w for w in wcalled if w not in defined]
        print("%s: names called %d; undefined: %s; wrappers called: %s; wrappers undefined: %s"
              % (name, len(called), " ".join(missing) or "none", " ".join(wcalled) or "none",
                 " ".join(wmissing) or "none"))
    DEFINED
    echo "command: python3 -I -B <scratch>/w/defined.py '[ cmp true' <scripts>/$(basename "$SELF"), and the same over a copy of this script with one planted call of an undefined helper, over a planted script calling an undefined helper through is, and over a planted script that calls yn and defines neither yn nor ynnot (the program printed below; rulings Z, AD and AK a; change NF41)"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/defined.py"
    python3 -I -B "$B/defined.py" "[ cmp true" "$SELF" >"$B/def-self.out" 2>"$B/def-self.err" </dev/null
    def_rc=$?
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/def-self.out"
    echo "  exit $def_rc; stderr bytes $(wc -c <"$B/def-self.err")"
    def_self_ok() { [ "$def_rc" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$B/def-self.err" ] && [ "$(count_matches -F '; undefined: none; wrappers called: yn ynnot; wrappers undefined: none' "$B/def-self.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "every helper a yn, ynnot, is or isnot call of this script names is defined in it, and yn and ynnot, the two it calls, are themselves defined (rulings Z, AD and AK a; change NF41)" "$(yn def_self_ok)"
    { cat "$SELF"; printf '%s\n' "zz=\$""(yn zz_planted_undefined_helper)"; } >"$B/def-plant.sh"
    python3 -I -B "$B/defined.py" "[ cmp true" "$B/def-plant.sh" >"$B/def-plant.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    echo "  over the planted copy: $(cat "$B/def-plant.out")"
    def_plant_ok() { [ "$(count_matches -F '; undefined: zz_planted_undefined_helper; ' "$B/def-plant.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check names the one planted undefined helper in a copy of this script (ruling Z)" "$(yn def_plant_ok)"
    printf '%s\n' 'is() { :; }' "x=\$""(is f)" >"$B/def-is.sh"
    python3 -I -B "$B/defined.py" "[ cmp true" "$B/def-is.sh" >"$B/def-is.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    echo "  over a planted script defining is and calling is f: $(cat "$B/def-is.out")"
    def_is_ok() { [ "$(count_matches -F '; undefined: f; wrappers called: is; wrappers undefined: none' "$B/def-is.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check reads an is call and names its undefined helper (ruling AK a)" "$(yn def_is_ok)"
    printf '%s\n' 'f() { :; }' "x=\$""(yn f)" >"$B/def-noyn.sh"
    python3 -I -B "$B/defined.py" "[ cmp true" "$B/def-noyn.sh" >"$B/def-noyn.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    echo "  over a planted script defining f and calling yn f: $(cat "$B/def-noyn.out")"
    def_noyn_ok() { [ "$(count_matches -F '; wrappers called: yn; wrappers undefined: yn' "$B/def-noyn.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a planted script that calls yn and defines neither yn nor ynnot (ruling AD)" "$(yn def_noyn_ok)"
    # Change NF42 (planning's verification of P1, ruling D): this script's own
    # placeholder check, the scan's rule, printed with its planted controls:
    # every lower-case angle-bracketed token printed before a slash, and every
    # scrub target of a sed s# expression, is declared by a root line saying
    # the token stands for something. The planted tokens are built from
    # pieces, so this text holds none.
    ph_used() {
      {
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E 's#[^#]*#<[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*>' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E '<[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*>$'
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E '<[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*>/' "$1" | sed 's#/$##'
      } | LC_ALL=C sort -u
    }
    ph_declared() {
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -E '(^|echo ")root: ' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E '<[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*>(/[a-z0-9]+)? stands for' |
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E '^<[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*>' | LC_ALL=C sort -u
    }
    ph_undeclared() { LC_ALL=C comm -23 <(ph_used "$1") <(ph_declared "$1") | count_lines /dev/stdin; }
    PH_L='<'
    printf 'echo "root: %srepo> stands for x"\necho "read %srepo>/a and %szzph>/b"\n' "$PH_L" "$PH_L" "$PH_L" >"$B/ph-bad"
    printf 'echo "root: %srepo> stands for x; %szzph> stands for y"\necho "read %srepo>/a and %szzph>/b"\n' "$PH_L" "$PH_L" "$PH_L" "$PH_L" >"$B/ph-ok"
    printf '  sed -e "s#$X#%szzscrub>#g"\necho "root: %srepo> stands for x"\n' "$PH_L" "$PH_L" >"$B/ph-scrub"
    echo "command: the scan's placeholder rule (the tokens printed before a slash and the sed scrub targets, less those a root line declares) over this script's own source, and over three planted files (planning's verification of P1, ruling D; change NF42)"
    echo "  this script: placeholders $(ph_used "$SELF" | tr '\n' ' '); declared by root lines $(ph_declared "$SELF" | tr '\n' ' '); undeclared $(ph_undeclared "$SELF")"
    check "every placeholder this script prints is declared by one of its root lines, by the scan's rule (ruling D; change NF42)" "$(yn [ "$(ph_undeclared "$SELF")" = 0 ])"
    echo "  planted: undeclared $(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-bad") in a file printing a token before a slash with no root line for it; $(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-ok") in the same file with the token declared; $(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-scrub") in a file with an undeclared scrub target"
    check "control: the same rule finds the planted undeclared token before a slash (ruling D)" "$(yn [ "$(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-bad")" = 1 ])"
    check "control: the same rule finds none once the planted token is declared" "$(yn [ "$(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-ok")" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same rule finds the planted undeclared scrub target" "$(yn [ "$(ph_undeclared "$B/ph-scrub")" = 1 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits by role, read from git"
    by_subject() { git log --format='%H' -n 1 -F --grep="$1"; }
    REC=$(by_subject 'M6 part 6 P2 record: the logs, the records, the check, the scan')
    DOC1=$(by_subject 'M6 part 6 P3: commit planning docs (the P2 verification and rulings)')
    CODE1=$(by_subject 'M6 part 6 P3: a sheet add on a workbook root binding no relationships prefix')
    # Change NA60: two earlier commits the carried statements read, each by its
    # full subject: M6 part 5 P2's phase commit (the tool's main.rs) and M6
    # part 5 P2's base, P1's record commit (the containers' old text, change
    # NC57).
    P2PHASE=$(by_subject 'M6 part 5 P2: openpyxl-ops.py named-style')
    P2BASE=$(by_subject 'M6 part 5 P1 record: the logs, the records, the check, the scan')
    echo "command: git log --format=%H -n 1 -F --grep=<the role's full subject>, for each role"
    echo "  M6 part 6 P2's record commit (the base): ${REC:-none}"
    echo "  the doc commit: ${DOC1:-none}"
    echo "  the code commit, the phase commit (specs/0043 decision 3 A, ruling M): ${CODE1:-none}"
    echo "  M6 part 5 P2's phase commit: ${P2PHASE:-none}; M6 part 5 P2's base, P1's record commit: ${P2BASE:-none}"
    echo "command: git rev-parse <phase commit>~0 to <phase commit>~2"
    for k in 0 1 2; do git rev-parse "$C~$k"; done | sed 's/^/    /'
    roles_in_order() {
      local r k=0
      for r in "$CODE1" "$DOC1" "$REC"; do
        [ -n "$r" ] || return 1
        [ "$(git rev-parse "$C~$k")" = "$r" ] || return 1
        k=$((k + 1))
      done
    }
    check "the code commit, the doc commit and the base, each the next one's parent, the code commit the phase commit (change NA60)" "$(yn roles_in_order)"
    roles_ctl() { local CODE1=$DOC1; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc commit named as the phase commit (change NA60)" "$(ynnot roles_ctl)"
    roles_ctl2() { local REC=$DOC1; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc commit named as the base" "$(ynnot roles_ctl2)"
    p2_parents() { [ -n "$P2PHASE" ] && [ -n "$P2BASE" ] && git merge-base --is-ancestor "$P2PHASE" "$REC" && [ "$(git rev-parse "$P2PHASE~4")" = "$P2BASE" ]; }
    check "M6 part 5 P2's phase commit is an ancestor of the base and P1's record commit its phase's base, four commits before it (change NA60)" "$(yn p2_parents)"
    p2_parents_ctl() { local P2PHASE=$REC; p2_parents; }
    check "control: the same test refuses the base named as M6 part 5 P2's phase commit (change NA60)" "$(ynnot p2_parents_ctl)"
    # Change NA60: the full shas the phase's FACTS.md names for each role, and
    # the two earlier commits'.
    pinned_ok() { [ "$REC" = 3102354f7971f926c74ce5c3a42066d9213d0493 ] && [ "$DOC1" = 7f3b43c81511787d1b2cc8bb9c7c2bd8d9dab1c8 ] && [ "$CODE1" = 7ac8b74d8f280fbdc9bea0cc2cdf631e9d11a2ee ] && [ "$P2PHASE" = bf07f86f51f905c685e73f8880a98494068ee49b ] && [ "$P2BASE" = 02c467ea8e49164a597b68ad954af7dbf8bb0346 ]; }
    check "each role is the full sha <phase>/FACTS.md names for it, and M6 part 5 P2's phase commit and base theirs (change NA60)" "$(yn pinned_ok)"
    pinned_ctl() { local CODE1=$DOC1; pinned_ok; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the doc commit named as the phase commit (change NA60)" "$(ynnot pinned_ctl)"
    echo
    echo "phase: Milestone 6 part 6 P3 ($SPEC) negative.log; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    # Change NF41 (rulings AA and AK b): every attempt refused at entry, or
    # superseded, is named by RERUN_NOTE and each of its files hashed here,
    # with the directory it is kept in; the hashing is asserted, the run log's
    # form.
    # Change NF42 (planning's verification of P1, ruling F, and ruling AA's
    # keeping): every file RERUN_FILES names lies in <superseded>, and one of
    # them is the superseded script that wrote the attempt, a .sh file there;
    # checked on a rerun, their controls on every run.
    rerun_kept() { local sf; [ -n "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ] || return 1; for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do case $sf in "$SUPERSEDED_DIR"/*) ;; *) return 1 ;; esac; done; }
    rerun_script() { local sf; for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do case $sf in "$SUPERSEDED_DIR"/*.sh) return 0 ;; esac; done; return 1; }
    rerun_kept_ctl() { local RERUN_FILES="$SUPERSEDED_DIR/a.log $PHASE_DIR/b.log"; rerun_kept; }
    rerun_script_ctl() { local RERUN_FILES="$SUPERSEDED_DIR/a.log $SUPERSEDED_DIR/a.outer.stderr"; rerun_script; }
    rerun_script_ok_ctl() { local RERUN_FILES="$SUPERSEDED_DIR/a.log $SUPERSEDED_DIR/x/m6p6-p3-negative.sh"; rerun_script; }
    n_rerun_files=0
    n_rerun_missing=0
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above, with the directory it is kept in (rulings AA and AK b; change NF41)"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        n_rerun_files=$((n_rerun_files + 1))
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s  kept in %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        else
          n_rerun_missing=$((n_rerun_missing + 1))
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time (named in %s)\n' "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"; fi
      rerun_hashed() { [ "$n_rerun_files" -gt 0 ] && [ "$n_rerun_missing" = 0 ]; }
      check "every file of the attempt RERUN_NOTE names is hashed above, and RERUN_FILES names at least one (rulings AA and AK b; change NF41)" "$(yn rerun_hashed)"
      check "every file RERUN_FILES names lies in <superseded> (ruling AA; change NF42)" "$(yn rerun_kept)"
      check "RERUN_FILES names the superseded script that wrote the attempt, a .sh file in <superseded> (ruling F; change NF42)" "$(yn rerun_script)"
    fi
    check "control: rerun_kept refuses a RERUN_FILES naming a file outside <superseded> (change NF42)" "$(ynnot rerun_kept_ctl)"
    check "control: rerun_script refuses a RERUN_FILES naming no .sh file (ruling F; change NF42)" "$(ynnot rerun_script_ctl)"
    check "control: rerun_script takes a RERUN_FILES naming a .sh file in <superseded>" "$(yn rerun_script_ok_ctl)"
